    respective contract. Deviating terms and conditions of the Client apply only with the
    express consent of Ebmeyer Consulting, which must be given in text form.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Conclusion of Contract and Right of Withdrawal</h2>
  <p>
    Quotations from Ebmeyer Consulting are valid for 14 calendar days from the date of the
    quotation. The contract is concluded by written acceptance of the quotation (including
    by e-mail) or by signature of the order confirmation. For registrations via an online
    registration form or the platform of a cooperation partner, the contract is concluded
    upon confirmation of the registration by Ebmeyer Consulting.
  </p>
  <p>
    The scope and content of the services result exclusively from the quotation or order
    confirmation. Services not listed there are not owed. Telephone or verbal agreements and
    commitments become binding only upon written confirmation by Ebmeyer Consulting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Consumers (B2C clients) have the right to withdraw from the contract with Ebmeyer
    Consulting within 14 days of its conclusion. The deadline is met if the Client notifies
    Ebmeyer Consulting of the withdrawal in good time. Withdrawal may be declared in
    particular by e-mail to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. The Client
    may use the <a href="#withdrawal-form">model withdrawal form in the annex</a> to these
    General Terms and Conditions, but is not required to do so. No reason needs to be given
    for the withdrawal. To exercise the right of withdrawal, it is sufficient for the Client
    to send the notice of withdrawal before the 14-day period expires. Exercising the right
    of withdrawal results in the unwinding of the contract.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any payment already made will be refunded to the Client within 14 days of receipt of the
    withdrawal by Ebmeyer Consulting. Ebmeyer Consulting will use the same means of payment
    for this refund as the Client used for the payment.
  </p>
  <p>
    The right of withdrawal expires before the end of the 14-day period if performance of
    the service has begun with the Client's express consent, the Client has confirmed
    awareness that the right of withdrawal will be lost upon full performance of the
    contract by Ebmeyer Consulting, and Ebmeyer Consulting has fully performed the service.
    If the Client withdraws from the service contract in good time before Ebmeyer
    Consulting has fully performed the service, the Client owes compensation for the value
    of the services rendered by Ebmeyer Consulting up to the time of withdrawal.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Services</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting provides AI strategy consulting for companies, SMEs, self-employed
    persons and private individuals, multi-phase consulting programmes, workshops, training
    sessions and courses both online and on site, keynotes and presentations, teaching
    assignments, and the design and configuration of individual AI assistants on existing
    third-party platforms.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ongoing consulting as well as workshops, training sessions, courses, keynotes and
    presentations are generally rendered as a mandate under Art. 394 et seq. of the Swiss
    Code of Obligations (CO). Where individual work results are expressly designated as
    deliverables capable of acceptance, the provisions on contracts for work under Art. 363
    et seq. CO may apply. The specific legal qualification of the contract depends on the
    agreed subject matter of the services. No guarantee of success, in particular regarding
    revenue, cost or efficiency targets, is owed unless expressly agreed.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting may engage partners to perform the services and remains the Client's
    point of contact in such cases. Services that the Client agrees and settles directly
    with third parties, in particular technical implementation, licences, hosting or
    services of third-party platforms, are not part of the contract.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting does not provide legal, tax, financial or medical advice. All
    entrepreneurial decisions are taken by the Client on its own responsibility.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Client's Cooperation</h2>
  <p>
    The Client provides, in good time and in full, all information, documents and access
    required for the performance of the services and designates a contact person authorised
    to take decisions. The Client handles queries and agreed preparatory tasks within the
    agreed deadline. The Client is responsible for the accuracy and legal admissibility of
    the information, documents, data, content and access it provides.
  </p>
  <p>
    For on-site appointments, the Client provides suitable premises, a stable internet
    connection, the necessary presentation equipment and – in the case of training sessions
    – working devices for the participants.
  </p>
  <p>
    Delays attributable to the Client extend the agreed dates accordingly. Where this
    results in additional work beyond the agreed scope of services, such work is quoted
    separately and performed only after written approval.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Appointments, Rescheduling and Cancellation</h2>
  <p>
    The following cancellation rules apply only to individual appointments confirmed in
    writing or to an event date expressly designated as such. The Client may reschedule or
    cancel a confirmed appointment. Rescheduling is deemed a cancellation unless an
    alternative date is agreed. In the event of cancellation or rescheduling due to illness,
    Ebmeyer Consulting may request suitable evidence, without restricting mandatory
    statutory rights. In the event of technical disruption to an online appointment, Ebmeyer
    Consulting offers a reasonable alternative date. The following flat rates constitute
    liquidated damages.
  </p>
  <p>In the event of cancellation by the Client, the following applies to the fee:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>up to 14 calendar days before the appointment: no charge</li>
    <li>13 to 7 calendar days before the appointment: 50 per cent of the fee agreed for the appointment concerned</li>
    <li>less than 7 calendar days before the appointment or in the event of non-attendance: 100 per cent of the fee agreed for the appointment concerned</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Third-party and travel costs already incurred and no longer cancellable are payable in
    addition only if they were stated in the quotation or approved in advance by the Client.
  </p>
  <p>
    If Ebmeyer Consulting definitively cancels an appointment, payments already made for the
    cancelled appointment are refunded, unless an alternative date or crediting towards an
    equivalent service is agreed. Third-party or travel costs already incurred and no longer
    cancellable may be charged only if they were stated in the quotation or approved in
    advance by the Client. Mandatory statutory claims remain reserved. Claims for damages
    are excluded.
  </p>
  <p>
    Sessions not taken within a multi-part programme expire 12 months after the start of the
    programme, provided the Client is responsible for not taking them and no mandatory
    statutory claim, in particular following termination under Art. 404 CO, precludes this.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Fees and Payment</h2>
  <p>
    All prices are in Swiss francs and exclusive of value added tax. Ebmeyer Consulting is
    currently not liable for VAT. Should VAT liability arise, VAT will be charged in
    addition.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a fixed fee is agreed, remuneration covers the scope of services defined in the
    quotation. The fee is determined by the scope, complexity and value of the services, not
    by the actual time spent. There is no entitlement to a reduction if less time is
    required. If more time is required within the agreed scope of services, there is no
    entitlement to additional remuneration.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a time-based fee is agreed, remuneration is calculated according to the time spent
    (hourly fee).
  </p>
  <p>
    Not included in the fee are travel and accommodation costs, licence and tool costs,
    services of engaged third parties, and printing, material and room costs. For on-site
    appointments, the travel flat rate stated in the quotation is charged.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unless otherwise agreed, the fee is payable in full before the first appointment. The
    first appointment takes place only after receipt of payment. For multi-phase
    programmes, the fee for each phase is payable in full before the first appointment of
    that phase. Workshops, seminars and presentations are payable in full before the event
    date. Payment in instalments is possible by prior agreement in text form. The amount and
    due dates of the instalments are set out in the quotation or order confirmation; the
    first instalment is payable before the first appointment. If an instalment remains
    unpaid despite a reminder and the setting of a reasonable grace period, the entire
    outstanding balance becomes due immediately.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unless another period is agreed, invoices are payable within 14 calendar days of the
    invoice date without deduction. Once payment is due, default interest of 5 per cent per
    annum is owed (Art. 104 CO). From the second reminder onwards, Ebmeyer Consulting may
    charge a reasonable flat-rate administrative fee of CHF 30.– as lump-sum compensation
    for reasonable costs. In the event of payment default, Ebmeyer Consulting may suspend
    performance of the services after a prior reminder and the setting of a reasonable
    grace period.
  </p>
  <p>
    Discounts or special conditions apply only to the specific individual order designated
    and create no entitlement in respect of subsequent orders.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Revision Rounds and Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    The fee includes one revision round per service unit. Feedback shall be provided in
    consolidated form and in writing within 10 working days of performance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Further revision rounds as well as changes or extensions to the scope of services are
    not included in the fee and are subject to charge. They are quoted separately and
    carried out only after written approval.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deliveries or services expressly designated as capable of acceptance are deemed accepted
    if the Client does not raise a written and comprehensible objection to apparent defects
    within 10 working days of delivery. Mere productive use does not constitute
    unconditional acceptance where it evidently serves the testing or trial of the
    deliverable. This deemed acceptance does not apply to ongoing consulting, workshops,
    presentations or individual sessions. Mandatory statutory rights and statutory
    limitation periods remain unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Rights of Use</h2>
  <p>
    All rights to the methods, models, templates, rule sets, prompt and system
    architectures, training materials and presentations contributed or developed by Ebmeyer
    Consulting remain with Ebmeyer Consulting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Upon full payment, the Client receives a non-exclusive, non-transferable right of
    unlimited duration to use the deliverables created for it within its own organisation or
    for its own purposes.
  </p>
  <p>
    Without written consent, the following are not permitted in particular: transfer or sale
    to third parties, use for the Client's own paid consulting or training offerings, and
    use for training AI models.
  </p>
  <p>
    Recordings of workshops, training sessions and presentations require prior written
    consent. Course materials are intended exclusively for the personal use of participants.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Client warrants that it holds the necessary rights to all materials it provides and
    indemnifies Ebmeyer Consulting against third-party claims to the extent that these are
    based on a culpable breach of this warranty by the Client.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Use of Artificial Intelligence</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting uses artificial intelligence systems and third-party tools to perform
    its services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Results produced by AI-supported systems are generated on a probabilistic basis and may
    be incomplete, outdated or factually incorrect. They must be reviewed by the Client
    before any productive or otherwise legally relevant use. Ebmeyer Consulting exercises
    reasonable care in the selection, use, configuration and monitoring of the systems
    employed, but gives no guarantee as to the accuracy, completeness, currency or
    availability of AI-generated content. The liability provisions in Section 12 and
    mandatory law remain unaffected.
  </p>
  <p>
    The availability, functionality, pricing and terms of use of third-party tools are
    beyond the control of Ebmeyer Consulting. The terms of the respective providers remain
    decisive, in particular regarding data use and model training. Ebmeyer Consulting
    guarantees neither the availability nor the unchanged continuation of these services.
    The Client obtains any required licences and subscriptions in its own name and at its
    own expense.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Client ensures that no sensitive personal data, professional or official secrets,
    health data and no data relating to children or young people are entered into AI
    systems, unless expressly agreed in writing. Without such an agreement, the processing
    of such data is excluded from the scope of services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Following handover of an AI assistant, operation, maintenance, monitoring and updating
    are the responsibility of the Client. Support and further development are owed only
    under a separate agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Confidentiality and Data Protection</h2>
  <p>
    Both parties treat non-public information of the other party as confidential and use it
    solely for the performance of the contract. Excluded from this is information that was
    already lawfully known to the receiving party, becomes public without breach of this
    obligation, is lawfully received from third parties without an obligation of
    confidentiality, or must be disclosed on the basis of a statutory, official or court
    order. To the extent legally permissible, the receiving party informs the other party
    before any such disclosure. At the request of the other party, confidential information
    must be returned or deleted, unless statutory retention obligations prevent this. This
    obligation applies for the term of the contract and for three years after its end. For
    trade secrets, it applies for as long as they require confidentiality.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting processes personal data in accordance with the Swiss Federal Act on
    Data Protection (FADP) and, where applicable, the GDPR. Details are set out in the
    <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a> at www.ebmeyer-consulting.ch.
  </p>

  <h2>11. References</h2>
  <p>
    Ebmeyer Consulting may use the Client's name and logo as well as a general,
    non-confidential description of the collaboration as a reference only with the Client's
